    "d47c4f90-b1c6-4c61-b423-ca2d0ff09475": {
      "type": "columns-1",
      "blocks": {
        "f5938453-db6a-4623-a83b-d73529cf89af": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Bonus #1: Yoga Therapists",
            "text": "<h3>Get 30 Continuing Education Credits</h3><p>This course is 30 hours of approved professional development for the continuing education of Certified Yoga Therapists via the International Association of Yoga Therapists (IAYT).</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/yoga-nidra-iayt-approved.jpg",
            "dropdown_text": "",
            "background_color": "",
            "text_color": ""
          }
        },
        "46ac2460-c747-4067-823b-d062702f351e": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Bonus #2: Teachers",
            "text": "<h3>Get 20 Continuing Education Credits </h3><p>Yoga Alliance requires all yoga teachers to accumulate at least 30 hours of continuing education every three years. 20 online hours are allowed to count toward this requirement.</p><p>Fulfilling 20 of these study hours is as easy as logging into the Yoga Alliance website and entering your hours after you’ve completed iRest Yoga Nidra Meditation Level 1 Teacher Training. Continue your yoga education with this course and more from the Yoga International library!<br/></p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/yoga-nidra-yoga-alliance.png",
            "dropdown_text": "",
            "background_color": "",
            "text_color": ""
          }
        },
        "6b7d24e3-8868-4464-9e76-e240561f2e17": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Bonus #3: Healthcare Professionals:",
            "text": "<h3>Get 27.5 Clinical Continuing Education Credits</h3><p>CE credits for healthcare professions are provided by the Spiritual Competency Resource Center (SCRC), which is co-sponsoring this program and maintains responsibility for this program and its content. The SCRC is approved by the American Psychological Association, the California Board of Behavioral Sciences, and the California Board of Registered Nursing (BRN Provider CEP16887). RNs, LCSWs, MFTs, and other mental health professionals from other states or provinces will need to verify with their licensing board about whether or not they accept programs offered by approved sponsors of CE by the above licensing bodies. For more information, click here.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/yoga-nidra-scrcLogo.jpg",
            "dropdown_text": "",
            "background_color": "",
            "text_color": ""
          }
        },
        "c44c4c41-f434-44a2-94de-5c5db501bf27": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "BONUS #4 LIVE ONLINE Q&As",
            "text": "<h3><strong>3x Live Q&As with Institute Founder & In-House Nutritionist</strong></h3><p>As you begin the program, it’s normal to have lots of questions and be seeking extra guidance. We’re providing that support in real-time with 3 intimate Q&A sessions with Food Matters Institute Co-Founder, Laurentine and our in-house nutritionist and student advisor, Kayla. (Recordings available if you’re unable to attend the sessions live.)</p><p><strong>Valued at: $498</strong> - Yours Free</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/cert-bonus-online-live-qa-lk.jpg",
            "dropdown_text": "",
            "background_color": "",
            "text_color": ""
          }
        }
      },
